cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use te-drift-detector in your work, please cite it as below."
title: "te-drift-detector: cross-turn scaffold/state drift detection for agent sessions"
abstract: >-
  A standard-library Python tool that detects gradual scaffold/state drift across
  the turns of an agent conversation. It fingerprints per-turn features (facts,
  entities, sentiment, task framing, authority, register, negation, vocabulary),
  measures drift against a baseline and turn-to-turn velocity, and flags
  sustained corruption that looks clean turn-by-turn. Ships with an eval harness
  that runs known scaffold-corruption strategies through the detector.
type: software
authors:
  - name: "Hermes Labs"
license: MIT
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-07-06"
repository-code: "https://github.com/hermes-labs-ai/te-drift-detector"
keywords:
  - large-language-models
  - agents
  - drift-detection
  - multi-turn
  - evaluation
  - monitoring
